    {
      "block_id": "h2-2",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Current Hardening Status",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-3",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "SearchReplace is largely complete:",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-4",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- structured invocation/result/receipt models: present - `build_receipt()`: present - schema coverage: present - content-light validator coverage: present - receipt index compatibility: present - automatic receipt emission through the agent loop: present",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-5",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Remaining Gaps",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-6",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "1. **End-to-end agent-loop test** - Current evidence proves `build_receipt()` and generic receipt emission separately. - Missing: a full synthetic agent-loop test that exercises `_execute_tool()` end to end.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-7",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "2. **Sanitizer edge cases** - `refusal_reason` and `warnings` are sanitized, but the current audit still flags the need for a tighter regression around any future contextual text.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-8",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "3. **Structured failure completeness** - Some `ToolError` paths still bypass receipt emission because they are caller/setup errors rather than tool outcomes. - That is acceptable, but should remain explicit and tested.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-9",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "4. **Status completeness** - Structured statuses are present, but the audit should keep checking that every intended status emits a receipt and indexes correctly.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-10",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Evidence Standard",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-11",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "SearchReplace should remain the reference pattern for deterministic mutation tools:",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-12",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- content-light receipts - schema coverage - policy validation - receipt index compatibility - structured refusals",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-13",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Next Step",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-14",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Use SearchReplace as the baseline template for `write_file`.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    }
  ],
